Conference Event Scheduling using Java Interface
 Description
This project demonstrates the implementation of an interface in Java. An interface named Schedulable is created with a method called scheduleEvent(). The ConferenceEvent class implements the interface and provides the functionality to schedule and display conference event details.

 Objective

To understand and implement the concept of interfaces in Java using the Schedulable interface and ConferenceEvent class.

Technologies Used
Java
Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
 Program Structure 

Schedulable – Interface containing the scheduleEvent() method.
ConferenceEvent – Class that implements the Schedulable interface.
main() – Creates an object and calls the scheduleEvent() method.

Program Code

interface Schedulable {
    void scheduleEvent();
}

class ConferenceEvent implements Schedulable {

    public void scheduleEvent() {
        System.out.println("Conference Event Scheduled");
        System.out.println("Event Name: Java Technology Conference");
        System.out.println("Venue: Main Auditorium");
        System.out.println("Date: 25 September 2026");
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ConferenceEvent event = new ConferenceEvent();
        event.scheduleEvent();
    }
}

 Output

Conference Event Scheduled
Event Name: Java Technology Conference
Venue: Main Auditorium
Date: 25 September 2026

Concepts Used

Interface
Method Implementation
implements Keyword
Class and Object
Method Calling

 How to Run

Save the program as ConferenceEvent.java.
Compile the program:
javac ConferenceEvent.java
Run the program:
java ConferenceEvent

 Conclusion

This program successfully demonstrates how a Java interface can be implemented in a class. The ConferenceEvent class implements the Schedulable interface and provides the implementation for the scheduleEvent() method.
